    "problem": "This paper addresses the claim that satellite data shows a \"leveling off of warming\" over the last two decades by systematically analyzing tropospheric temperature trends and evaluating their statistical significance relative to natural internal climate variability.",
    "method": "The authors propose a statistical significance test comparing observed satellite tropospheric warming trends against a distribution of trends from climate model simulations of natural internal variability to evaluate claims of a recent \"leveling off\" of warming.",
    "task": "This paper tests the claim of a \"leveling off of warming\" over the past two decades by comparing observed satellite tropospheric temperature trends with climate model estimates of trends arising from natural internal variability.",
